ases, while DR Congo continues to battle its deadliest outbreak of the disease.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20672002626114fba9573e25626b1a4cdc0642454d19ccc5aacedec002b53bcf</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tundu Lissu: After escaping the death penalty, what does his guilty verdict mean for Tanzania's democracy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:314ee9bfd900e4152faed3f427eda0f09b8b971ce3d8ab87ce0cb441eb6ab3c3</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democr/a-79908512--3044020567d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democracy/a-79908512?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A treason trial could have meant death by hanging for Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu. Instead, he now faces four years in prison for incitement to unrest. Can voices of dissident truly be heard in the country?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a9f3d5e84ef4570563b7e229b4af6215519f7d2b4af2842418eaf4bc2793da0</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
